    "note": "ITU Region 1 (Europe, Africa, the Middle East west of the Persian Gulf, and the former Soviet Union). Frequency limits read from the Region 1 column of the Table of Frequency Allocations in Article 5 of the ITU Radio Regulations, Edition of 2024 (in force 1 January 2025, incorporating WRC-23), cross-checked against the FCC Online Table of Frequency Allocations (47 CFR 2.106, revised 1 July 2022), which reproduces the same International Table. Amateur band edges are the Region 1 ITU allocations, not national licence limits: 160 m is 1810-1850 kHz (RR 5.96 lets named countries add up to 200 kHz inside 1850-2000 kHz at 10 W, which is why many national plans show 1810-2000), and 6 m is the 50-52 MHz secondary allocation created by WRC-19. Shortwave broadcast edges are the Region 1 broadcasting allocations including the WARC-92 extension segments flagged by RR 5.134; the tropical bands carry the RR 5.113 conditions and are used only in the tropical zone. CEPT-specific entries (PMR446 per ECC/DEC(15)05, the 863-870 MHz SRD band per ERC/REC 70-03, TETRA/PPDR per ERC/DEC(96)01 and ECC/DEC(08)05, DAB blocks per the Band III channel raster) apply across CEPT rather than the whole of Region 1; the DAB block edges are DERIVED from the published block centre frequencies plus the 1.536 MHz DAB signal bandwidth, as no source prints them directly. INFORMATIONAL ONLY - a display aid, not an authoritative or licensing reference. National variations within the region are not modelled. JSON has no comment syntax, so this note lives in the data; the loader ignores unknown keys.",
